    <worksheet margin="1in" bottom="1.25cm" xml:id="hilbert-spaces-complete">
    <title>Hilbert Spaces (Complete)</title>
        <page>
        
            <exercise workspace="2in">
            <title>Motivation</title>
                <statement>
                    <p>
                
                    </p>
                </statement>
                <solution>
                    <p>
                        Vector spaces are important because these are the general spaces wave functions live in.
                        However, we also need some additional structure for comparing wave functions and guaranteeing
                        that we can combine wave functions in natural ways and still have a valid wave function.
                    </p>
                </solution>
            </exercise>

            <exercise workspace="6in">
            <title>Hilbert Space</title>
                <introduction>
                    <p>
                Wave functions live within a <term>Hilbert Space</term>, which 
                
                    </p>
                </introduction>
                <task workspace="1in">
                    <statement>
